# API keys for recording the VCR cassettes of the tests, and for the live runs
# of dev/evals/. Most contributors need no .env file: without one, the tests set
# dummy keys and replay the recorded requests (see "VCR Cassette Management" in
# CONTRIBUTING.md).
#
# Copy this file to .env, then uncomment and fill in the variables of the APIs
# that your tests call. As long as .env sets no variable, the tests still set
# the dummy keys. Once it sets one, they set none: CONTEXTGEM_OPENAI_API_KEY and
# CONTEXTGEM_TYPESAFE_API_KEY then need a value, any value if you only replay
# their tests, as litellm rejects a request without a key before it can be
# replayed. The other variables fall back to dummy values when they are not set.

# OpenAI: most tests of LLMs, the Decisions API of OpenAI, the usage examples
# CONTEXTGEM_OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Anthropic: the tests test_anthropic_llms_* in tests/test_llms.py
# CONTEXTGEM_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# TypeSafe: the tests of decision models that call typesafe/jev-latest
# CONTEXTGEM_TYPESAFE_API_KEY=

# Microsoft Foundry: the tests of the decision model deployed in a Foundry
# resource as ms-decision-model. The endpoint is the one of the resource:
# https://<resource>.services.ai.azure.com
# CONTEXTGEM_AZURE_AI_API_KEY=
# CONTEXTGEM_AZURE_AI_API_BASE=
